     "path": "/news/playing-games-to-heal-kids/",
     "role": "blog",
     "commentLink": "Comment",
     "excerpt": "<p>Hey guys, some of you may have heard about the <a href=\"http://extralife.sarcasticgamer.com/wp/\">ExtraLife charity.</a>  Basically its a 24 hour videogame marathon taking place on Oct. 16th.  I am raising money for Primary Children&#8217;s Medical Center in Salt Lake City, if you have a few extra bucks to spare, head on over to <a href=\"/page/4/ https:/www.hospitalshelpingkids.org/ExtraLife/m.aspx?i=188784752AED36FD3\">this site and send a few bucks their way</a>, it&#8217;s for a good cause.</p>\n<p>There are other ways you can help too!  If you don&#8217;t have the cash, or want to otherwise get involved the entire event is open to anyone who wants to participate.  <a href=\"https://www.hospitalshelpingkids.org/ExtraLife/\">Sign up</a> and create your own team here (you can even choose the hospital of your choice for the funds to be donated to when you sign up)</p>\n<p>For any other information, you can take a gander at the offical ExtraLife charity site <a href=\"http://extralife.sarcasticgamer.com/wp/\">here</a></p>"
    }
